Research OS hypothesize route, not yet applied
================================================

Two hunks, both unified diffs against `bucket-foundation` PR #6's own
`feat/research-os-k12-phase0` branch (verified to apply cleanly against
that branch's real file content, 2026-09-10):

1. `src/lib/research-os/types.ts`: adds `HypothesizeResult` and its three
   supporting interfaces, the shape `src/app/api/research-os/hypothesize/
   route.ts` below returns.
2. `src/app/api/research-os/hypothesize/route.ts`, new file: `POST
   {productionId}` loads the caller's own production (an ownership check
   this patch adds on purpose, closing the same gap PR #6's own
   `production/route.ts` POST handler left open, named in that PR's
   review), forwards it to `hte-serve` on `127.0.0.1` with a timeout, and
   returns the trimmed, camelCased result.

Apply with `git apply tools/hypothesis-engine/docs/research-os-hypothesize-
route.patch` from the bucket-foundation repo root, after PR #6 has merged
and `src/lib/research-os/types.ts` exists on `main`. This file stays
unapplied until then; it becomes its own PR once PR #6 lands, per the task
that produced it (see `tools/hypothesis-engine/docs/PRODUCTION-SCHEMA-
ALIGNMENT.md`'s own closing section).

Env this route reads: `HTE_SERVE_URL` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8420`),
`HTE_SERVE_TIMEOUT_S` (default `20`). Start `hte-serve` alongside the
Next.js app in fake mode to exercise this route without the `claude` CLI:

    cd tools/hypothesis-engine
    python3 -m hte.serve --port 8420 --fake

